  "notes": "{聞|き}かす is a transitive godan verb. It functions as the causative form of {聞|き}く, though it is a distinct lexical item rather than a grammatical causative.\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{聞|き}かせている indicates an ongoing action of telling or playing something for someone to hear.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- [person]に[thing]を{聞|き}かせる (tell someone something)\n- [person]に{聞|き}かせる (let someone hear)\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {話|はなし}を{聞|き}かせる (tell a story)\n- {歌|うた}を{聞|き}かせる (sing a song for someone)\n- {読|よ}み{聞|き}かせる (read aloud to someone)\n\nThe て form {聞|き}かせて is very common in conversation: いい{話|はなし}を{聞|き}かせてよ (Tell me a good story). The compound {読|よ}み{聞|き}かせ is a standard term for reading aloud to children.",
